{"id":"173c7353-8f13-47d9-bcb5-8ac50434cec6","object":"chat.completion","created":1784996112,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core_dist = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    \\n    # Build edges with mutual reachability weight\\n    edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        if u not in core_dist or v not in core_dist:\\n            raise ValueError('Unknown node in distance entry')\\n        w = max(core_dist[u], core_dist[v], d)\\n        # canonicalize: store (min, max) so each undirected edge only once\\n        if u < v:\\n            edges.append((w, u, v))\\n        else:\\n            edges.append((w, v, u))\\n    \\n    # Sort by weight, then by first node, then second node\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    \\n    # Union-Find (Disjoint Set Union) with path compression and union by rank\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    \\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    \\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    \\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    required = n - 1\\n    \\n    for w, u, v in edges:\\n        if len(mst_edges) == required:\\n            break\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n    \\n    if len(mst_edges) != required:\\n        raise ValueError('Graph is disconnected; cannot form spanning tree')\\n    \\n    return {\\n        'mst_edges': mst_edges,\\n        'total_weight': total_weight\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to generate the Python implementation code for solve(case) that takes a payload (as per the fixture) and returns a JSON object with mst_edges and total_weight. The structural schema is given. The algorithm: compute core distances from the case's \"core_distance\" dict, mutual reachability for each pair as max(core_left, core_right, distance). Then sort edges by mutual reachability, then by node IDs (string comparison presumably). Then run Kruskal's algorithm with union-find (disjoint set union) to select edges until we have |nodes|-1 edges. If not enough edges (graph disconnected) raise ValueError. Also ensure we use the exact node IDs from \"nodes\" list. The output mst_edges should be list of [node1, node2, weight] where weight is the mutual reachability distance (float). Total weight sum of those weights. Must not mutate input. Use only standard library. No randomness. The output must be JSON-serializable.\n\nImplementation details: parse case[\"nodes\"], core_distance dict, distances list of [node1, node2, distance]. For each distance entry, compute mutual_reachability = max(core_distance[node1], core_distance[node2], distance). Then create edge tuple (weight, node1, node2). Sort edges by (weight, node1, node2) where node1 < node2? Actually we need canonicalize undirected endpoints so that we store as (min, max) to avoid duplicates. In the input distances list, each pair appears only once? Likely yes, but still canonicalize. Then sort by weight, then node1, then node2 (strings). Then run DSU: parent dict initially each node its own parent, rank dict. For each edge in sorted order, find roots of node1 and node2; if different, union, add to mst_edges list, add weight to total. Stop when len(mst_edges) == len(nodes)-1. If after processing all edges we have fewer, raise ValueError (disconnected). Return dict with \"mst_edges\" (list of [node1, node2, weight]) and \"total_weight\".\n\nBe careful: node IDs are strings like \"p0\", \"p1\", etc. Comparison with string is fine. No custom comparator needed.\n\nThe output schema requires exactly those two keys, no additional. Return as dict.\n\nWrite solve function inside implementation string. The candidate_artifact text provides guidance.\n\nWe cannot import any external libraries; only standard library.\n\nWe must return JSON object with implementation key.\n\nNow produce the response."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2017,"completion_tokens":1097,"total_tokens":3114,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1920},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":537},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1920,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":97},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}